# A compatible pair in the day care, one step short of the egg check.
#
# The pair has to be male and female and the lab cannot ask for a gender:
# Pokemon_GiveMonFromScript rolls a personality and SpeciesData_GetGenderOf
# reads the low byte of it against the species' ratio. These three Bibarel are
# the mint's own first, second and third rolls, and of them the first is male
# and the third female, so those two go in and the spare male stays in the
# party. Deposits are by party slot AFTER the ones before them have left, which
# is why the second line says 1.
#
# Same species and the same trainer gives PARENTS_MED_COMPATIBILITY, which is
# the best a lab-minted pair can reach: PARENTS_MAX wants two different
# original trainers and every mon here has the player's. That score is then
# rolled against `LCRNG_Next() * 100 / 0xffff`, so half the frames the counter
# could wrap on produce no egg at all, 254 was one of them and lost, 250 wins
# on the fifth step of the walk. Nothing here is random; the frame the wrap
# lands on is, and that is what the preload picks.

name BREEDER
gender GENDER_MALE
trainer-id 10412
money 9000
badge BADGE_ID_COAL
badge BADGE_ID_FOREST
party SPECIES_BIBAREL 25 ITEM_NONE
party SPECIES_BIBAREL 26 ITEM_NONE
party SPECIES_BIBAREL 27 ITEM_NONE
daycare 0
daycare 1
daycare-steps 1 250
map MAP_HEADER_SOLACEON_TOWN 0x236 0x291 FACE_DOWN
